.TH SENTINEL-SIGN 1 "March 2026" "Sentinel-CC v4.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sentinel-sign \- Sentinel-CC Ed25519 binary signing tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sentinel-sign
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIBINARY\fR \fIPRIVATE_KEY\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sentinel-sign
computes a cryptographic hash over the security-relevant ELF sections
of a Sentinel-CC instrumented binary and writes an Ed25519 signature
into the binary's .signature section.
.PP
The hash covers the concatenation of:
.RS
.nf
SHA-256(.text || .sentinel || .sentinel_cfi || .sentinel_imports)
.fi
.RE
.PP
This creates a tamper-evident binding between the executable code and
its embedded security policy. Any modification to code or policy
after signing will cause signature verification to fail at load time.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-v
Print version string and exit.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I BINARY
Path to the ELF binary to sign. Must have been compiled with the
Sentinel LLVM pass (contains .sentinel, .sentinel_cfi, and .signature
sections).
.TP
.I PRIVATE_KEY
Path to the Ed25519 private key in PEM format.
.SH KEY GENERATION
Generate an Ed25519 keypair with OpenSSL:
.PP
.nf
openssl genpkey -algorithm Ed25519 -out priv.pem
openssl pkey -in priv.pem -pubout -out pub.pem
.fi
.PP
Or use the Makefile:
.PP
.nf
make keys
.fi
.SH SIGNED SECTIONS
.TP
.B .text
Executable code section.
.TP
.B .sentinel
Syscall policy array (generated by LLVM pass).
.TP
.B .sentinel_cfi
CFI caller-range metadata (generated by LLVM pass).
.TP
.B .sentinel_imports
External function import list (generated by LLVM pass). Optional —
only present in dynamically-linked binaries.
.TP
.B .signature
Output: 64-byte Ed25519 signature written in-place.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Binary signed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Error (missing section, invalid key, I/O failure).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Sign a binary
./sentinel-sign victim priv.pem

# Sign after compilation in a build script
clang -fpass-plugin=SentinelPass.so -O2 app.c -o app
./sentinel-sign app /etc/sentinel/priv.pem
.fi
.SH KEY ROTATION
To rotate keys and re-sign all binaries:
.PP
.nf
sudo make key-rotate
.fi
.PP
This revokes the current key (appends its SHA-256 fingerprint to
/etc/sentinel/revoked_keys), generates a new keypair, and re-signs
all victim and attack binaries.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sentinel-loader (1),
.BR openssl-genpkey (1),
.BR openssl-pkey (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Nevin Shine (System Security Student)
.SH BUGS
